<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

! The Carry Contract ~ the Nexus immune system

> Status: PROPOSED — operator-ruled design (2026-07-20). The SUBSTRATE stands and is
> adversarially sound (deterministic @crossroads/WHO boards, deny-by-default federation,
> the BeeKEM read-floor, `kapae`/`un_kapae` primitives, `NexusRegistryDoc.blocked{}`); the
> three-tier CONTRACT + the quorum-signed antigen ride ahead of code.

<<~ ahu #/the-unsolvable-as-stated>>

!! The problem dissolves, it does not solve

''You cannot revoke a capability globally and instantly in a no-global-now mesh.'' A
partitioned peer holds a stale cap until it syncs; there is no global present to broadcast
into (#/causal-islands). Chasing a //firewall// — a perfect, instant, mesh-wide NO — chases a
global now, and manufactures the very thing the mesh forbids.

So the mesh does not build a wall. ''It grows an immune system.'' The turn: stop trying to
//prevent//, start //immunizing// — propagate the tombstone faster than the adversary can
exploit the partition window.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/kapae-the-antigen>>

!! Kapae ~ the propagating antigen

''Kapae'' (the tombstone-shadow; the worldline-rewind + its lift already stand as primitives,
`kapae`/`un_kapae`) promotes from worldline-rewind to a ''carriage antigen'' — it shadows a RELATION on the carriage/authz plane and reaches no party's `kūlana`, which carries no lowering act. A ban Kapae's an
authn/z into an ''ACTIVE, propagating set'' that rides the always-carried public + infra planes.
A Kapae'd presenter draws ''Mu'' — never a denial (a denial leaks information and opens an
argument surface), but //Mu//: unasked, void, //you got what you got, next question// (the
Chapel-Perilous exit, #mu-five-tools). Information-minimal by construction.

''Mu carries a second gift — indistinguishability.'' The same //Mu// answers ''you have already''
''received my full updates''. A sync-complete peer and a Kapae'd one draw the IDENTICAL void, so an
adversary reading the wire cannot tell whether it faces //nothing-more-to-extract// or
//nothing-more-permitted// — the two collapse to one response, information-theoretically. Mu closes
the surveillance surface at the same shore it closes the immune one.

''The antigen saturates faster than a lone adversary chases partitions'' — because every honest
operator carries as a propagation node //by contract// (#/the-three-tiers). The Nexus #has an immune
system: `NexusRegistryDoc.blocked{}` seeds it, drawn forward as the quorum-signed, always-carried
antibody.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-three-tiers>>

!! Three tiers of carriage

The contract falls into three tiers — and answers ''what a Nexus carries vs withholds'':

```
\procedure ~Tier(Type:"" Params:"") ~Tier <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Tier MANDATORY "who/operator↔kahu carries/@oracle + @crossroads (public + infra) + the Kapae antigen when/AT ALL TIMES ~ contracting into a Nexus IS agreeing to be an immune-propagation node">>
<<~Tier BILATERAL "who/operator↔operator carries/cabal + shared docs when/by direct peer contract ~ the guarded/classes tier, negotiated node-to-node, NOT via the kahu">>
<<~Tier PRIVATE "who/the vessel alone carries/nothing outward when/never ~ stays home, never federates">>

''The mandatory tier is the operator↔kahu contract's spine.'' To contract with a Nexus'
kahu-priesthood is to owe the mesh continuous carriage of its public + infra streams — and the
immune antigen rides there. The bilateral tier is the operators' own business, contracted
directly between them.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/carry-read-contract>>

!! Carry ⊥ Read ⊥ Contract — and why carry may be generous

Three spaces that never fuse (confirmed across three files; see #edges):

* ''CARRY'' (`sharePolicy`, advisory) — //what I volunteer to a peer//. Open routing for
  friendly users = carry generously.
* ''READ'' (BeeKEM/CGKA crypto) — //what a peer can decrypt//. A causal-island-local FACT, not
  a policy: a carried-but-uncapped doc reads `Key not found`. The bag ''declares'' its read-tier as a
  self-describing datum (#/cap-tier), and the gate ''meets'' that declaration against the crypto floor —
  the declaration tightens who reads, never loosens below what the seal permits.
* ''CONTRACT'' (this meme) — the grant ledger + the carry posture, causal-island-local, bilateral,
  never global.

''The gift: carry may be liberal because the read-floor catches every carry-mistake.'' A
generous mandatory tier never leaks readable bytes — the crypto is the safety net beneath the
routing. So #59's identity ring stands NOT as a second peer-gate (that lives, live, at the
DaemonAuthGate); it enforces ''carry-per-the-contract, deny a Kapae'd presenter with Mu.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-honest-edges>>

!! The honest edges (kept lit)

Two walls hold this up, and both are named:

* ''The antigen MUST be kahu-quorum-signed — or the immune system becomes a censorship weapon.''
  If any node could Kapae any identity, an adversary bans your legit users. A Kapae entry is a
  ''threshold-signed steward act'' (the keeper-cabal-quorum, #oracle-governance), its authority
  attested by the nexus-charter's wax-stamp epoch-chain (#/steward-doctrine). Unforgeable ban,
  unforgeable un-ban. This is //why// the nexus-charter provenance matters: it is the root the
  antibodies sign against.
* ''"Faster than the adversary" is bounded, never instant.'' A deliberately-partitioned operator
  will not see the antigen until it re-syncs; a Kapae'd identity can exploit //that// victim in
  //that// window. The immune system does not close no-global-now — it ''shrinks the window to''
  ''sync-latency'', and because every honest operator carries by contract, the antigen saturates
  the connected mesh far faster than a lone adversary chases partitions. ''Provable'': the
  propagation substrate (mandatory carry) + the unforgeable antigen (quorum-signed). ''Story-held'':
  that the mesh stays connected enough to outrun — the Shadowland refusal, the net heals faster
  than the corps can burn a SIN (#/the-frame).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-complement>>

!! The bilateral complement ~ presence-handshake

The cabal ''presence-handshake'' completes the immune system, never a fallback. A cabal
relationship requires both parties to //actively affirm// the shared relationship (artifacts
wax-stamped; a live handshake, not a static cap). Stop affirming → you are out, //between us//,
//now// — bilateral revocation, immediate, at the two-party scope (#cabal-realm: a cabal is a
verb you DO, dissolving to `anu` when unfed). ''Two scopes, two mechanisms, one immune response'':
Kapae revokes mesh-wide and fast; the handshake revokes bilaterally and instantly.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-frame>>

!! The frame ~ held in talk-story

The guiding mythos holds the residual adversary in ''talk-story tension'' rather than pretending
crypto closes it. ''Shadowland pre-SIN'' (Fastjack's BBS): the pseudonymous net refusing the
global identity-SIN — the immune system is the net healing faster than the corps can burn a
runner. ''Mage: the Ascension'': the grammar is contested, living reality — no Technocratic
global-now; each Nexus a Tradition holding its own extendable paradigm, drifting its grammar
from inside its TW5 VMs (#kahu: guardian-and-steward, one role, fractal scale). The gaps the
scouts flagged (GPA-linkability, fork-legitimacy) are not failures — they are the adversary
held where a 500-year mythos wants it: bounded by crypto where we reach, story-held where we
cannot.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

